  "properties": {
    "long_instructions": "# Interactivity in Web Apps\r\n\r\n#### When you visit a website or open an app, you’re not just looking at information—you’re doing something with it. \r\n#### Interactivity is what turns a static page into an engaging experience. It’s what allows users to click, tap, type, scroll, or hover to make something happen.\r\n\r\n<details style=\"background:#f7f8fa; padding:20px; border-radius:10px; box-shadow:0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); margin:20px 0;\">\r\n  <summary style=\"font-size:16pt; font-weight:bold; cursor:pointer;\">\r\n    ⚡ Interactive Elements in Web Apps\r\n  </summary>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"margin-top:15px; line-height:1.6;\">\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size:14pt;\"><strong>Interactive elements come in many forms:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul style=\"padding-left:20px;\">\r\n      <li style=\"font-size:14pt;\"><strong>Buttons</strong> that trigger actions</li><br>\r\n      <li style=\"font-size:14pt;\"><strong>Menus</strong> that expand or collapse</li><br>\r\n      <li style=\"font-size:14pt;\"><strong>Search bars</strong> that respond as you type</li><br>\r\n      <li style=\"font-size:14pt;\"><strong>Icons</strong> that change color or shape when hovered over</li>\r\n    </ul>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size:14pt; margin-top:15px;\">\r\n      These small moments of feedback and response are what make a web app feel alive and user-friendly.\r\n    </p>\r\n\r\n  </div>\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"background-color: #B7E0E5; border-radius: 10px; padding: 15px; margin: 20px auto; max-width: 85%; box-sizing: border-box; word-wrap: break-word; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 120%;\">📖 <strong> Interactivity</strong> is the ability of a software application or website to respond to user input.\r\n</p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n--- \r\n\r\n> #### Take a look at the website image below and think about where you might see elements of interactivity.\r\n\r\n<div style=\"\r\n  display: flex;\r\n  justify-content: center;\r\n  align-items: center;\r\n  max-width: 1000px;\r\n  margin: 20px auto;\r\n\">\r\n  <img \r\n    src=\"https://images.code.org/582df09f74b0f4858ad96c0b75d045f0-image-1760992309979.png\" \r\n    alt=\"amazon website 2025\"\r\n    style=\"width: 80%; max-width: 800px; height: auto; border-radius: 12px; box-shadow: 0 6px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.25);\"\r\n  >\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Reflection\r\n\r\n>- #### Where do you notice interactive elements?\r\n>- #### How might those interactions help or guide the user?\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
